      "text": "Stabilization in the braid groups I: MTWS — 41 sections: Front matter; Introduction; The problem\n\n**Stabilization in the braid groups I: MTWS**\n\n*JOAN S BIRMAN*\n\n128 pp, 41 sections.\n\n**Outline.** Front matter; 1 Introduction; 1.1 The problem; 1.2 Block-strand diagrams and templates; 1.2.1 The two destabilization templates; 1.2.2 The admissible flype templates; 1.2.3 The exchange move template and sequences; 1.2.4 The cyclic templates; 1.2.5 The G–flype and G–exchange templates; 1.3 Statement of results; 1.4 Plan of the paper; 2 Getting started; 2.1 The basic construction for knots; 2.2 The general case; 2.3 A key example of the basic construction; 3 Introducing braid foliations; 3.1 Braid foliations of Seifert surfaces; 3.2 Control over the foliations",
